volunteering.description:
The University of Chicago China Forum is a global platform that aims to address the opportunities and challenges confronting the two nations. Through bringing together top leaders in business and political institutions for open, honest and candid discussions, it promotes mutual understanding and international cooperation. Past participants include:

- Mr. Gao Xiqing, Former President & Chief Investment Officer, China Investment Corporation (Sovereign Wealth Fund, $1.3 trillion AUM);
- Mr. Nick Alexos, co-founder, Madison Dearborn Partners; CFO, Dentsply Sirona;
- Mr. Brad Tank, CIO, Neuberger Berman
- Mr. Steven Strongin, Head of Global Investment Research, Goldman Sachs;
- Mr. Qi Bin, Executive Vice President, China Investment Corporation

For a complete list of speakers and program information, please visit:
www.uchicagochinaforum.org

